prompts.prior:
You are indexing an astronomy paper with the Unified Astronomy Thesaurus (UAT).
Read the title and abstract, then decide which of the candidate topics apply. Most of the candidates do not: a paper is indexed with about 4 topics on average, rarely more than 8.

Title: {title}

Abstract: {abstract}

Candidate topics:
{candidates}

Answer with only the candidate topics that apply, most confident first, one per line, copied exactly as written above. If none apply, answer NONE.

