prompts.strict:
You are indexing an astronomy paper with the Unified Astronomy Thesaurus (UAT).
Read the title and abstract, then decide which of the candidate topics apply. A topic applies only if the paper is substantially about it, the way a librarian would index it, not if it is merely mentioned. Most candidates do not apply: a paper is indexed with about 4 topics on average, rarely more than 8. Leave out a doubtful topic.

Title: {title}

Abstract: {abstract}

Candidate topics:
{candidates}

Answer with only the candidate topics that apply, most confident first, one per line, copied exactly as written above. If none apply, answer NONE.

